Keep one task pointer, one wait queue, one atomic pending count, and one borrowed
rk_state pointer in execution/worker.c.

The proc callback checks actions_enabled before calling rk_worker_request(). The
request operation adds one unless pending is already INT_MAX, then wakes the
wait queue. The thread waits for pending > 0 or kthread_should_stop(), checks the
stop condition first, and consumes one unit with atomic_dec_if_positive().

Start the worker before publishing procfs. On publication failure and unload,
kthread_stop() must return before state is destroyed.
